1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,850
Papol gives you two ways to make notes
while you read.

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:10,050
First, choose Anchor, then click beside the exact place
you want to remember.

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:13,400
Open My anchors and select Add a note.

4
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:16,850
Write your thought, then save it to the anchor.

5
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:22,825
Now click Back to Papol. On the paper page,
the same note appears under Notes.

6
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:29,325
Anchors work best when a thought depends
on one precise passage or diagram.

7
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:37,000
For the second method, highlight text to save a passage.
For a figure, choose Clipper and draw a box around it.

8
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:42,625
Select the clip's Send button, add your note,
choose a board, and send it to that board.

9
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:49,475
Open the board and drag the saved figure
onto the canvas.

10
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:53,700
Boards gather evidence across papers for comparison.

11
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,350
Anchors keep context. Boards connect.
Enjoy Papol.
